# WS2-04. # Sources: spec/05-statements.md STMT-11/STMT-12 and spec/03-ownership.md §5: defer joins the cleanup ladder; drops and defers run in reverse registration order on every normal exit edge (return, break, continue, scope end), not on a fault.
A defer in a loop body runs at each iteration's exit, including
# continue and break, before the iteration's local drops.
profiles: host
with: tok.clo
expect: output
contrast: if (i == 2) ==> if (i == 1)
contrast-expect: output
--- output
tail
d
drop 0
d
drop 1
d
drop 2
end
--- contrast-output
d
drop 0
tail
d
drop 1
d
drop 2
end
